    "created_at": "2025-05-26T21:17:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-05-26T21:17:22Z",
    "body": "Thanks for clarifying (here and through GVC): we essentially want to \"forward\" the user interaction on a browser surface (which is \"the permission prompt\" in this case) to the related renderer here.  I missed the user interaction on the permission prompt itself!  I am taking back my main concern.\n\n@annevk's concern above still applies, and I would suggest adding to [this list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#activation-triggering-input-event) something like \"a trusted ping\" representing user interaction on a connected browser-dialog.\n\n@annevk:\n- Does it sound like the abstraction you suggested?\n- Is there a link to the WebRTC case you mentioned?",
