    "created_at": "2025-06-16T20:13:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-16T20:13:11Z",
    "body": "> I believe the question boils down to - should the spec note that transient activation should not be conferred if the capturing Web app becomes too occluded? Or just unfocused? Or is this fine?\n\nWe need to be careful with this, \"forwarding\" user activation means allowing access to all user activation-gated APIs, which can sometimes confuse users when those actions are triggered from a background window (e.g., opening a popup or a file picker).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
